        <definition>static void Jobs::run</definition>
        <argsstring>(int count, Function &amp;&amp;function)</argsstring>
        <name>run</name>
        <qualifiedname>Jobs::run</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>count</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>Function &amp;&amp;</type>
          <declname>function</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs function once for each index in <computeroutput>[0, count)</computeroutput> and joins all workers. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Workers take the indexes from one atomic counter. The calling thread works too. The worker count is <computeroutput>min(count, juce::SystemStats::getNumCpus())</computeroutput>. One item, or one worker, runs on the calling thread alone.</para>
<para>A thread that cannot start is not an error. The work then runs on the threads that did start.</para>
<para>When a worker throws, that worker stops. After all workers join, the failure of the lowest-numbered failed worker is thrown again in the calling thread.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Function</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Callable accepting a single <computeroutput>int</computeroutput> item index. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>count</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of work items; must be non-negative. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>function</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Callable invoked concurrently from worker threads; caller synchronizes shared state. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
